 "amendments": {
  "items": {
   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to authorize certain police officers to receive certain service credit\nunder sections 384 and 384-d of the retirement and social security law",
    "basePrintNo": "S5785",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S5785-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "",
    "lawSection": "Retirement",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S5785\n\nSPONSOR: MAYER\n \nTITLE OF BILL:  An act to authorize certain police officers to receive\ncertain service credit under sections 384 and 384-d of the retirement\nand social security law\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThis bill will allow Jonathan Roman, David Arroyo, and Vincent Fiumara,\npolice officers employed by the Village of Port Chester, to participate\nin the New York state and local retirement system under the provisions\nof section 384-d of the retirement and social security law, and will\nallow Jason Behar, a police officer employed by the Village of Port\nChester, to participate in the New York state and local retirement\nsystem under the provisions of section 384 of the retirement and social\nsecurity law.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 of the bill provides that Jonathan Roman, David Arroyo, and\nVincent Fiumara, police officers employed by the Village of Port Ches-\nter, may be given full credit in the special twenty year retirement plan\ncontained in section 384-d of the retirement and social security law.\nThis change shall be made effective upon the election of the Village of\nPort Chester to assume the costs of such service and by making certain\nfilings with the state comptroller.\n\nSection 2 of the bill provides that Jason Behar, a police officer\nemployed by the Village of Port Chester, may be given full credit in the\nretirement plan contained in section 384 of the retirement and social\nsecurity law. This change shall be made effective upon the election of\nthe Village of Port Chester to assume the costs of such service and by\nmaking certain filings with the state comptroller.\n\nSection 3 sets an immediate effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nPolice Officers Jonathan Roman, David Arroyo, and Vincent Fiumara became\nemployed by the Village of Port Chester on August 4, 2014. At that time,\nthrough no fault of their own, they were enrolled in the New York state\nand local retirement system retirement plan under section 384 of the\nretirement and social security law, however, it was their desire to\ninstead enroll in the New York state and local retirement system retire-\nment plan under section 384-d of the retirement and social security law.\n\nPolice Officer Jason Behar became employed by the Village of Port Ches-\nter on May 26, 2015. At that time, through no fault of his own, he was\nenrolled in the New York state and local retirement system retirement\nplan under section 384-d of the retirement and social security law,\nhowever, it was his desire to enroll in the New York state and local\nretirement system retirement plan under section 384 of the retirement\nand social security law.\n\nThis bill credits the service of the above-named officers to date in the\nNew York state and local retirement system retirement plan under the\nsections of the retirement and social security law that such officers\ndesired.\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNone\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nNone to the state. Fiscal note attached.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
